   126  /* Remap the GDBM file so that its mapped region ends on SIZEth byte.
   127     If the file is opened with write permissions, FLAG controls how
   128     it is expanded.  The value _REMAP_DEFAULT truncates SIZE to the
   129     actual file size.  The value _REMAP_EXTEND extends the file, if
   130     necessary, to accomodate max(SIZE,dbf->header->next_block) bytes.
   131     Finally, the value _REMAP_END instructs the function to use
   132     max(SIZE, file_size) as the upper bound of the mapped region.
   133
   134     If the file is opened read-only, FLAG is ignored and SIZE is
   135     truncated to the actual file size.
   136
   137     The upper bound obtained that way is used as a *hint* to select
   138     the actual size of the mapped region. which can never exceed
   139     dbf->mapped_size_max.
